it.<br /> <br /> Any idea on a start time? Is it going to be on this site?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T16:52:21-07:00","id":436417,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with going through Avarice, but I'd personally prefer something tailored to the group. Of course, if the Storyteller is more comfortable with it, then Avarice will be a good idea.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with doing it on this site, if everyone else is. We will need an online dice-roller, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:58:47-07:00","id":436587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/434177-looking-for-pbp-want-to-try-out-a-mummy-the-curse-game?p=436417#post436417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm okay with going through Avarice, but I'd personally prefer something tailored to the group. Of course, if the Storyteller is more comfortable with it, then Avarice will be a good idea.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with doing it on this site, if everyone else is. We will need an online dice-roller, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Reading through the first part, it doesn't really fit as an introduction chronicle. I'd change it and make it more noobie friendly. It's something more for a later Chronicle. I like the ideas and I'll shamelessly steal some of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:47:50-07:00","id":437222,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with this being on these forums. If any other forum is preferred, maybe Rpol? As for online dice rollers, there's plenty available. I think the Umbral Echoes dice roller can work.<br /> <br /> I've deliberately not read through the Avarice Chronicle so it was just a suggestion. I'm perfectly happy to play something more tailored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:01:45-07:00","id":437673,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming everyone is going to be a mummy, but if someone wants they can instead play a cultist. I also think we should set the chronicle in Washington DC. Any objection too that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:18:33-07:00","id":437686,"title":"","content":"No objection at all. Do you think we should find a couple more players?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:36:22-07:00","id":437699,"title":"","content":"I might be interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T19:51:16-07:00","id":437918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/434177-looking-for-pbp-want-to-try-out-a-mummy-the-curse-game?p=437699#post437699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be interested.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to join. Anything you need to know?<br /> <br /> As for dice rollers, I've heard this one is good but I'm open: <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgroller.com/nwod/index.php</a><br /> <br /> We should also decide on mood and maturity. Anyone against anything like gore, sex, and all the fun stuff?<br /> <br /> Finally, we should discuss framework, how you're all connected. The standard game is the Allied Dead, you're all part of a meret (group of mummies) which I think would be best. If you want to get experimental, we can also do the pyramid or rotating pyramid option. That's where one player plays the role of the mummy and the others are cultists, while the rotating pyramid is whenever the mummy falls back to sleep or dies one of the other players takes over the role of the mummy. That's just something I thought I'd include for sake of completeness. The best choice would be the Allied Dead, everyone gets to be a badass mummy (unless you want to play a cultist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T03:14:47-07:00","id":438230,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with any level of mood and maturity.<br /> I'd also prefer Allied Dead.<br /> <br /> Oh, and by the way, are there any house-rules you had in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 03-12-2015, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T12:28:05-07:00","id":438778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/434177-looking-for-pbp-want-to-try-out-a-mummy-the-curse-game?p=438230#post438230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and by the way, are there any house-rules you had in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any house rules for mummy, I do have an update to God-Machine rules if you guys want to try that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:15:29-07:00","id":438888,"title":"","content":"I think I would like to do play by post for Mummy. Standard character creation rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T14:22:15-07:00","id":438894,"title":"","content":"No objection to playing in DC. That would mean the characters' tombs would in the city or its vicinity, yes?<br /> <br /> That dice roller looks fine. No objections here. I'm also fine with any level of maturity.<br /> <br /> I sent you a PM regarding a character idea I had, so I'm going to hold off on saying anything more in that regard. Allied Dead means sharing a cult, right?<br /> <br /> I'd be interested in seeing an update to the 2nd ed rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T15:06:26-07:00","id":438943,"title":"","content":"I'm currently in the process of designing a character as I type. Mesen-Nebu and Bull-Headed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T15:20:26-07:00","id":438952,"title":"","content":"You can all have your own cults if you want, or a mixing of two players sharing a cult while another player has their own cult. If you want a big cult, it would be best to share points with your allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T15:33:58-07:00","id":438987,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm thinking of a Serpent-Headed Sesha-Hebsu. Do mummies from different guilds share cults? I don't have any issue with sharing by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/480-blind-dragon","name":"Blind Dragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T15:44:51-07:00","id":438996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blind Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/434177-looking-for-pbp-want-to-try-out-a-mummy-the-curse-game?p=438987#post438987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm thinking of a Serpent-Headed Sesha-Hebsu. Do mummies from different guilds share cults? I don't have any issue with sharing by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Many mummies of different guilds share or merge cults together to better help each other out with their unique skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:12:18-07:00","id":439015,"title":"","content":"I'm currently trying to get involved in a Werewolf 2e PBP, but I've got the time and the spare character lying around that I'm definitely also open to a mummy game. Any spots left? Also, would you prefer I PM the character sheet and ideas? Oh, are we doing standard creation or this GMC update? I'd be up for trying it if it works. From what I hear Mummy is a serious pain to try and adapt to it. I'm good with us being a meret. One more question, will our characters have any starting Experience(s)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1705,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","user":"Okami","date":". 03-12-2015, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T17:44:41-07:00","id":439138,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind trying out a Jackal-Headed Su-Menent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T20:08:28-07:00","id":439280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/434177-looking-for-pbp-want-to-try-out-a-mummy-the-curse-game?p=439015#post439015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently trying to get involved in a Werewolf 2e PBP, but I've got the time and the spare character lying around that I'm definitely also open to a mummy game. Any spots left? Also, would you prefer I PM the character sheet and ideas? Oh, are we doing standard creation or this GMC update? I'd be up for trying it if it works. From what I hear Mummy is a serious pain to try and adapt to it. I'm good with us being a meret. One more question, will our characters have any starting Experience(s)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your welcome to join if you can. I'm finalizing the character stuff, so that should be up here soon. Then we can all decide if these updates will work for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:12:10-07:00","id":439482,"title":"","content":"These are rules I've cobbled together from other ideas from various forums and my own thoughts. If anything looks off, don't be afraid to say so.<br /> <br /> Starting mummies get 5 XP.<br /> <br /> Experience Costs<br /> Attributes - 4 XP<br /> Skills - 2 XP<br /> Skill Specialties - 1 XP<br /> Merits - 1 XP per dot<br /> Willpower Dots - 1 XP<br /> <br /> Guild, Decree or Judge Favored Affinity - 4 XP<br /> Fated Guild, Decree or Judge Favored Affinity* - 3 XP<br /> Other Affinity - 5 XP<br /> Fated Other Affinity* - 4 XP<br /> Utterances - 4 XP<br /> Defining Pillar - 1 XP<br /> Other Pillars - 2 XP<br /> Memory - 2 XP (At least 1 XP spent must be Sebayt XP)<br /> * The character may leave the choice of which Affinity to buy up to Fate. In these cases, the Storyteller, and not the player, determines which Affinity the character manifests.<br /> <br /> <br /> A mummies virtue and vice are fluid and can be swapped and changed with each descent at Memory 3 or lower.<br /> -Purpose (Virtue) \u2013 Your own personal view of yourself, changes very often with low memory.<br /> -Duty (Vice) \u2013 What others see you as because of how you present yourself. Doesn\u2019t change very often.<br /> <br /> Aspirations \u2013 It\u2019s very hard for a mummy to remember any personal goals they might have. Thus a mummy usually has all short term aspirations that are probably forgotten. However, long term goals may reveal themselves through play. You gain beats normally through these short term aspirations.<br /> -You have your purpose for awakening should be one of your aspirations.<br /> -Personal aspirations.<br /> <br /> Touchstones: It is hard for a mummy to gather a touchstone and they don\u2019t usually begin play with one (and even if they do, they probably won\u2019t remember). You gain one Touchstone at character creation. If you lose one of your Irem Touchstones or it is destroyed, you drop 1 dot of Memory. Modern Touchstones fade away all the time and you don\u2019t lose any Memory if they disappear through the flow of time. If the Touchstone is killed or destroyed, that may constitute a Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> -Irem Touchstones: a mummy has gathered a precious relic from the time of Irem and holds it deer. It might not even be a relic but a precious memory that the mummy works hard not to let go of. Or maybe it\u2019s a story your cultists tell to themselves. It can be anything that makes you long for your time in Irem. That being said, this touchstone probably has nothing to do with who you were in those times. The mortal person you were is long gone, but this gives you a little glimpse at better times that might not even have existed. If a character has a single attached Irem Touchstone, it adds a +2 die bonus to Breaking Point rolls. With multiple Irem Touchstones, add a +3 die bonus.<br /> <br /> -Modern Touchstones: These are the things that keep the mummy in the modern world. They are reminders that Irem is long gone and that it is a mummies job to move forward. It could be a valuable member of your cult or an attachment to a well-worn copy of The Great Gatsby. These Touchstones are different from Item Touchstones in that they don\u2019t bolster your Memory, but they do help your Willpower. If you spend time with your Modern Touchstone and bolster your attachment to it, you regain a Willpower point. If the defense of your Touchstone causes your serious harm you regain all spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> We are also playing with the Sanctity of Merit rules. This means that if you lose any Merit you currently have, be it an old cultist retainer that dies in an accident or is dead by your next descent, you can reallocate those dots to a new Merit (though you should try to have it make some sense for your mummy).<br /> <br /> <br /> Memory<br /> Sebayt Beats: In addition to any standard beats, you can also gain Sebayt Beats for showing acts or humanity. The Arisen also receive Sebayt beats for patient reconstitution of their souls, as represented by Pillars. Every time an Arisen reaches a new minimum rating in all Pillars - e.g., once she has at least ** in all Pillars - you gain 1 Sebayt beat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mention of Virtues and Vices in Affinities and Utterances<br /> Under the New World of Darkness Rules Revision (GMC) characters are no longer restricted to a small subset of Virtues and Vices. This creates some problems when adapting certain Affinities and Utterances from 1.0 rules. Barring a total rewrite of those abilities there is no hard fix for this, instead storytellers are suggested to follow the spirit of a character\u2019s virtue or vice. If it seems to fit under the umbrella of a particular Sin (as \u2018Vengeance\u2019 falls under \u2018Wrath\u2019) treat it as that sin for the purposes of that Affinity.<br /> <br /> <br /> For affinities and utterances, just choose the ones you want. I don't want to change any of them in any major way. We can work out how to update them to GMC later.<br /> <br /> So yeah, if everyone agrees on these updated rules I can make an OOC thread where every player can dump their character sheet and any other questions. Though we should probably establish who is all playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T06:50:48-07:00","id":439836,"title":"","content":"I would kind of prefer to stick to 1E as I haven't read MtC and the GMC update in ages nor have I played a game before using either so I'm already having to read through all the important bits again of the MtC rulebook. It will take me longer if I have to read through GMC as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T07:43:38-07:00","id":439908,"title":"","content":"I'm good with either ruleset, though I have to say I prefer GMC because its so much cleaner. As an aside Atsuki, GMC wouldn't really be that much of a burden as the major issue would be learning the new experience system, which is easy enough. Though perhaps we should stay to the 1e rules since this is Mummy. I would like to say I'm playing, that would be cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T18:31:42-07:00","id":440745,"title":"","content":"We can stick to 1e if everyone else agrees?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:45:48-07:00","id":440874,"title":"","content":"I think that would probably be easier, as much as I do like GMC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T22:47:53-07:00","id":440918,"title":"","content":"I think we're all in agreement except for Blind Dragon who I assume is fine using the regular rules (tell me if I'm wrong). I'll throw up the OOC Thread tomorrow so you all can brainstorm character concepts and post the final sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:21:53-07:00","id":441336,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I shall eagerly await the thread then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T14:19:46-07:00","id":441847,"title":"","content":"Is this still accepting new players? I would really like to play some Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T14:39:16-07:00","id":441852,"title":"","content":"We seem to have several players already, to be fair though, the nature of PBP's is for people to suddenly drop off the map without warning. Just take it up with our ST but I'm sure we'll be glad to have you!<br /> <br /> You can find our OOC Thread in the Play By Post subforum should you need to hash out character ideas, post the sheet, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T17:24:32-07:00","id":448519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/434177-looking-for-pbp-want-to-try-out-a-mummy-the-curse-game?p=441847#post441847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this still accepting new players? I would really like to play some Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we can fit you in. Still interested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T01:27:53-07:00","id":459754,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I didn't see this. While I might be too late now, I am definitely still interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","dat